  "body": "Closes #917\nClaim: cloud/i917-sonnet\n\n**Problem.** The viewer opened an `img3.super-h.fr` medium image (`<name>.md.<ext>`) as is: the screenshot stayed unreadable. The host's only rule removed `.th.`.\n\n**Change.**\n- `ImageHostRule.ThumbnailRewrite.fileNameMarker` → `fileNameMarkers(pathPrefix:markers:)`; the `img3.super-h.fr` rule now lists `[\".th.\", \".md.\"]`. Other hosts unchanged.\n- Other hosts: no medium rendition is sourced (no legacy `file:line` @ `87fe0d1c`, no capture), so no rule; listed as not sourced in HFR-PROTOCOL §LOT-056 and the LOT-056 spec.\n- Fallback: already in `ImageViewerModel.download` (full → the `shown` image, which is the medium here) and covered by `aMissingFullSizeImageFallsBackToTheThumbnailTheUserSaw`; nothing to add.\n- HFR-PROTOCOL §LOT-056 and the spec: medium shape recorded, labelled **code**, not verified. Source: `Classes/RehostImage.m:328-343` @ `87fe0d1c` (example Chevereto answer with `\"medium\"`), read at `:366-368`; the legacy upload-history sample is synthetic. Capture requested in #922.\n\n**Tests.** `ImageHostTableTests.img3MediumAndThumbnailBothOpenTheFullImage` (`.md.`, `.th.`, query kept, other URLs unchanged); shown to fail without the `.md.` marker (2 expectations fail, `swift test --filter ImageHostTableTests`). `ImageGalleryTests.anImg3MediumImage…` (app target, written on Linux, not built here: CI is the arbiter).\n\n### Ledger\n\n```changelog\n| T | Un aperçu médium img3 (.md.) s'ouvre en pleine taille dans la visionneuse. | #917 | `MessagesView.swift:3298-3312` @ `2440d79` and `87fe0d1c` (aucune règle `.md.`), `Classes/RehostImage.m:328-343, 366-368` @ `87fe0d1c` |\n```\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_014QH2CHo4bcnbt3rqVkPJ1o",
