   "body": "**Adversarial review (Opus 5.5, read-only sub-agent of cloud/orch; the author is Sonnet), verbatim:**\n\n> APPROVE — head 82447c38 (Opus 5.5 adversarial review of Sonnet work)\n>\n> Findings:\n> 1. Low. `docs/HFR-PROTOCOL.md:383` cites `samples/legacy-stores/upload-history-after-corrupt-rewrite.json` and `LegacyFormatsTests.swift:75` as the source of the `.md.` shape. The oracle README (`tooling/legacy-oracle/README.md:18,101`) says that sample is synthetic data. Legacy code has a firmer source: the example Chevereto answer in `Classes/RehostImage.m:328-343 @ 87fe0d1c` (`\"medium\": {\"filename\": \"example.md.png\", \"url\": \".../images/2014/06/04/example.md.png\"}`), which `RehostImage.m:366-368` reads. Failure scenario: a later reader judges the rule as resting on hand-written data only. Fix: add the `RehostImage.m` citation to the protocol line and to #922.\n> 2. Detail. The `### Ledger` proof cites `MessagesView.swift:3298-3312 @ 2440d79`. AGENTS.md §2 asks new citations to use `87fe0d1c`. Fix: add the matching range at `87fe0d1c`.\n>\n> Checked and sound:\n> - The img3 rule now removes both `.th.` and `.md.`.\n> - The other hosts' rules are unchanged.\n> - `isValidEncodedPath` still runs after the rewrite, and the invalid-path test still passes.\n> - `ImageViewerModel.download` (`ImageViewerModel.swift:185-188`) really does fall back to `shown`, and `aMissingFullSizeImageFallsBackToTheThumbnailTheUserSaw` covers it.\n> - The protocol entry is labelled **code**.\n> - #922 has the right labels (`host: mac`, `type: chore`), a Summary, acceptance criteria and `Refs #917`.\n> - No other open PR touches `ImageHost`.\n>\n> **Verified**\n> - `swift test --filter ImageHost`: 11 tests pass.\n> - With `.md.` removed from the marker list, `img3MediumAndThumbnailBothOpenTheFullImage` fails twice (lines 70 and 72).\n> - `ledger.py check-body --pr 923`: \"1 block(s) ok\".\n> - `swiftlint` on the changed files: no warnings.\n> - `ImageGalleryTests` (app target) was not built here: CI decides.\n\nThe sourcing matters here (AGENTS.md §3.1), so `cloud/i917-sonnet` makes one docs commit for items 1 and 2, followed by a short delta check.\n\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
